   "source": [
    "# Fine-tuning Public Investment Advisor AI Agent\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook fine-tunes the investment advisor AI agent using free financial data APIs and open-source LLMs.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Setup\n",
    "\n",
    "Install required packages:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%%capture\n",
    "!pip install transformers torch peft datasets tqdm\n",
    "!pip install matplotlib yfinance pandas\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Authentication & API Keys\n",
    "\n",
    "Get free API keys from:\n",
    "- **Finnhub**: https://finnhub.io (free tier: 30 requests/minute)\n",
    "- **Alpha Vantage**: https://www.alphavantage.co (free: 5 requests/minute)\n",
    "- **Yahoo Finance**: No key needed via yfinance\n",
    "\n",
    "Set environment variables in Colab:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import getpass\n",
    "\n",
    "FINNHUB_API_KEY = getpass.getpass(\"Enter Finnhub API key (or press Enter to skip):\").strip() or \"demo\"\n",
    "ALPHA_VANTAGE_API_KEY = getpass.getpass(\"Enter Alpha Vantage API key (or press Enter to skip):\").strip() or \"demo\"\n",
    "\n",
    "os.environ[\"FINNHUB_API_KEY\"] = FINNHUB_API_KEY\n",
    "os.environ[\"ALPHA_VANTAGE_API_KEY\"] = ALPHA_VANTAGE_API_KEY\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Finnhub key: {FINNHUB_API_KEY}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Alpha Vantage key: {ALPHA_VANTAGE_API_KEY}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load Free Financial Data\n",
    "\n",
    "Fetch market data, earnings, and financial metrics using free APIs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import yfinance as yf\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import requests\n",
    "\n",
    "# Example: Get AAPL stock data\n",
    "ticker = \"AAPL\"\n",
    "data = yf.download(ticker, start=\"2023-01-01\", end=\"2024-12-31\")\n",
    "print(f\"AAPL data shape: {data.shape}\")\n",
    "print(data.tail())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Prepare Training Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "Create instruction-following data for financial advice."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from datasets import Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "training_examples = [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"instruction\": \"Analyze AAPL stock performance and provide investment recommendation\",\n",
    "        \"input\": \"AAPL has shown 15% growth over 6 months with strong earnings. What should investors do?\",\n",
    "        \"output\": \"Based on the technical indicators and fundamentals, a Hold rating is recommended with target price of $185. Consider dollar-cost averaging for new positions.\"\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"instruction\": \"Evaluate TSLA investment opportunity\",\n",
    "        \"input\": \"TSLA trading at 25x P/E with growing EV deliveries. Is now a good time to buy?\",\n",
    "        \"output\": \"TSLA offers growth potential but valuations are rich. Consider a small allocation if seeking exposure to EV sector. Set stop-loss at $200.\"\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"instruction\": \"Compare VOO vs SPY ETFs\",\n",
    "        \"input\": \"Which is better for long-term growth: VOO or SPY?\",\n",
    "        \"output\": \"VOO has slightly lower fees (0.03% vs 0.09%) and similar performance. Both track S&P 500. VOO is preferred for cost-conscious investors.\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "dataset = Dataset.from_list(training_examples)\n",
    "print(f\"Training examples: {len(dataset)}\")\n",
    "print(dataset[0])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Fine-tune LLM with PEFT\n",
    "\n",
    "Use LoRA (Parameter-Efficient Fine-tuning) for efficient adaptation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM, AutoTokenizer, TrainingArguments\n",
    "from peft import LoraConfig, get_peft_model, TaskType\n",
    "from datasets import Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load base model (using a small model for Colab)\n",
    "model_name = \"microsoft/phi-2\"  # Small, Colab-friendly\n",
    "tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_name)\n",
    "tokenizer.pad_token = tokenizer.eos_token\n",
    "\n",
    "model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\n",
    "    model_name,\n",
    "    torch_dtype=\"auto\",\n",
    "    device_map=\"auto\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Configure LoRA\n",
    "lora_config = LoraConfig(\n",
    "    task_type=TaskType.CAUSAL_LM,\n",
    "    r=8,\n",
    "    lora_alpha=32,\n",
    "    lora_dropout=0.1,\n",
    "    target_modules=[\"q_proj\", \"k_proj\", \"v_proj\", \"o_proj\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "model = get_peft_model(model, lora_config)\n",
    "model.print_trainable_parameters()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Train the Investment Advisor\n",
    "\n",
    "Fine-tune on the financial dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from transformers import Trainer, TrainingArguments\n",
    "\n",
    "training_args = TrainingArguments(\n",
    "    output_dir=\"investment_advisor_model\",\n",
    "    num_train_epochs=3,\n",
    "    per_device_train_batch_size=4,\n",
    "    gradient_accumulation_steps=4,\n",
    "    learning_rate=2e-4,\n",
    "    weight_decay=0.01,\n",
    "    fp16=True,\n",
    "    logging_steps=10,\n",
    "    save_steps=50,\n",
    "    max_steps=-1,\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "trainer = Trainer(\n",
    "    model=model,\n",
    "    args=training_args,\n",
    "    train_dataset=dataset,\n",
    "    tokenizer=tokenizer\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "trainer.train()\n",
    "model.save_pretrained(\"investment_advisor_finetuned\")\n",
    "tokenizer.save_pretrained(\"investment_advisor_finetuned\")\n",
    "\n",
    print(\"Fine-tuning complete! Model saved to ./investment_advisor_finetuned\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Test the Fine-tuned Advisor\n",
    "\n",
    "Query the adapted model for investment advice."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM, AutoTokenizer\n",
    "\n",
    "model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\"investment_advisor_finetuned\")\n",
    "tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(\"investment_advisor_finetuned\")\n",
    "\n",
    "prompt = \"Analyze TSLA stock and provide investment advice:\"\n",
    "inputs = tokenizer(prompt, return_tensors=\"pt\").to(model.device)\n",
    "\n",
    "outputs = model.generate(\n",
    "    **inputs,\n",
    "    max_new_tokens=200,\n",
    "    temperature=0.7,\n",
    "    top_p=0.9,\n",
    "    do_sample=True\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "response = tokenizer.decode(outputs[0], skip_special_tokens=True)\n",
    "print(\"\\n--- Investment Advice ---\")\n",
    "print(response)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Deploy as API (FastAPI)\n",
    "\n",
    "Expose the fine-tuned model as a REST endpoint."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from fastapi import FastAPI\n",
    "from pydantic import BaseModel\n",
    "import uvicorn\n",
    "\n",
    "app = FastAPI(title=\"Investment Advisor AI\")\n\n\nclass Query(BaseModel):\n    question: str\n\n\n@app.post(\"/predict\")\nasync def predict(query: Query):\n    inputs = tokenizer(query.question, return_tensors=\"pt\").to(model.device)\n    outputs = model.generate(**inputs, max_new_tokens=200, temperature=0.7)\n    response = tokenizer.decode(outputs[0], skip_special_tokens=True)\n    return {\"response\": response}\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    uvicorn.run(app, host=\"0.0.0.0\", port=8000)\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "metadata": {\n "kernelspec": {\n  "display_name": \"Python 3\",\n  "language": \"python\",\n  "name": \"python3\"\n },\n "language_info": {\n  "name": \"python\",\n  "version": \"3.12\"\n }\n}\n